Dear Allen,

I was referring to section 7.7 of the MEDIPS Tutorial (or vignette) available at:
http://www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/vignettes/MEDIPS/inst/doc/MEDIPS.pdf

I recommend to apply the a PCA to the counts at the genomic windows returned by the MEDIPS.meth() function where you probably want to remove windows with zero or low counts first. Here, the assumption is that CpG density correction of MeDIP signals might not be necessary as you are comparing different samples with each other (please see section 7.7 of the MEDIPS tutorial). In case you want to apply a PCA on CpG density methylation estimates anyway, you can either use the rms values or calculate methylation estimates using  BayMeth, a recent tool that appears to be superior for such methylation estimates.

All the best,
Lukas

